A||N||35||johnmac||HOT - MUST DO V6 OWNERS||||1||
Z||000000||johnmac||08-30-2001||04:19 PM||||Checked my rear air cooling duct which directs air to the distributor & electronic components.<P>Was not working - Why?<P>Pulled the blower off the right side of the luggage compartment and checked it on the bench.<P>THE UNIT WAS WIRED WRONG FROM THE FACTORY.<BR>V6 Owners - - - Check on the bench first and if req'd cut the wires and join the black ground wire to the red/black power wire and vice-versa . This will change the rotation of the blower to the correct orientation.<P>If you don't you may fry your electronics over and over!!!<P>Thanks GM/Pontiac for dropping the ball again!<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Galen||08-30-2001||05:11 PM||||Perhaps someone just wired yours wrong<P>------------------<BR>Ray -   <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>   -<A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A> - AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||08-30-2001||05:30 PM||||Although I wouldn't recommend ripping them out, there is some question to their necessity.  All 88 V6's do not have the rear blower.  At least I don't have to check any on mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Maybe it was just a cost cutting measure, but I doubt GM would have done it if it would jeopardize component life... they did give out warrenties on these things after all.<P>Then again, I am talking about General Motors  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnmac||08-30-2001||05:43 PM||||TO GALEN <P>Nope - the wiring came from the factory and I have heard of other V6 owners have the same hookup. <P>It may affect the 88 models.<P>If you have a pre 88 V6 I would suggest you check it out. <P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
