Z||000011||Mach10||08-30-2001||07:37 PM||||I wouldn't assume that everyone is having similar luck. First of all, the operating temps of the internal components is only supposed to be around 165. Ogre has shown that underhood ambient temps go ABOVE 200. That's HOT. Again, read Ogres article. If you aren't having problems, then more power to ya. Otherwise, I consider the removal of the cooling fan as a bad mistake on GMs part.||||reg||7
