Z||000034||fieroluke||09-03-2001||06:45 PM||||Hi folks,<P>yes, the 88 V6 does not have the engine compartment fan anymore, and yes, this was a cost cutting measure. But not only is the heat shielding around the X-over pipe different, the EGR (a major source of heat to reach the distributor) is mounted in a different angle. This is why the 88 X-over pipe is different from the previous years. The other thing that is cooled in the pre 88's is the alternator, which received a special heat shield in 88. So, if you install the 88 alternator heat shield and the crossover pipe, along with a new EGR tube (which has a different angle too), and the 88 crossover heatshield, then you may be able to get away with dismantling the engine compartment fan.<P>I'd go a different route though: have that thing on all the time! The temp switch kicks in so late, it doesn't really help the alternator or distributor at all. Having it on all the time doesn't hurt, and may very well prolong the life of distributor and alternator.<P>Best regards,<P>-Oliver<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/mycars.jpg"> ||||reg||4
